00:29:41,660 --> 00:29:44,320
gives us that sort of shearing action that we really like when

554
00:29:44,420 --> 00:29:46,120
the blades are really close together.

555
00:29:46,220 --> 00:29:47,860
The closer they are and the sharper they are,

556
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:50,520
the better it does for shearing.

557
00:29:50,620 --> 00:29:52,460
The blades team together to create

558
00:29:52,461 --> 00:29:56,000
to create 15,000 times the shearing force of a single

559
00:29:56,100 --> 00:29:58,900
pair of scissors.

560
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:02,600
We've got about 35 or 40 cutters in this machine,

561
00:30:02,700 --> 00:30:06,340
so about 4,000 inches of scissor action.

562
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:08,840
And then if you look at this machine turning at about 20

563
00:30:08,940 --> 00:30:13,620
RPM, we have about a mile of scissor length that we're

