00:30:45,721 --> 00:30:51,220
The world's sharpest cutters don't have to be intricately

573
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:53,620
hardened and honed blades.

574
00:30:53,720 --> 00:30:57,960
Instead, they can be made from something that's not even solid.

575
00:30:58,060 --> 00:31:02,480
The cutting experts at Southern California's Hansen Steel

576
00:31:02,580 --> 00:31:07,340
Services carve through solid steel plate with a laser,

577
00:31:07,440 --> 00:31:11,940
an intense beam of microscopically focused light.

578
00:31:12,040 --> 00:31:15,720
It's the most effective tool for making exacting cutters

579
00:31:15,721 --> 00:31:20,020
in steel less than one inch thick.

580
00:31:20,120 --> 00:31:23,420
The sharpest industrial metal cut made by a laser

581
00:31:23,520 --> 00:31:27,060
can measure just 4,000ths of an inch across,

582
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:28,560
about as thin as a sheet of paper.

583
00:31:31,660 --> 00:31:34,680
Chances are that a laser has cut thousands of common steel

584
00:31:34,780 --> 00:31:37,680
