585
00:31:37,780 --> 00:31:40,120
from the components in your DVD player,

586
00:31:40,220 --> 00:31:43,380
to the stainless steel skins of modern kitchen appliances,

587
00:31:43,381 --> 00:31:47,620
to the sprockets and gears in your fishing reel.

588
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:51,720
Before industrial lasers came into their own in the 1980s,

589
00:31:51,820 --> 00:31:54,760
precision shaping steel relied on slower and less

590
00:31:54,860 --> 00:31:57,260
cost-effective methods.

591
00:31:57,360 --> 00:31:59,660
Parts had to be punched out by press

592
00:31:59,760 --> 00:32:03,600
or machined with skillful care.

593
00:32:03,700 --> 00:32:06,900
A laser generates its cutting beam by converting gases

594
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,540
into surgically precise energy.

595
00:32:08,541 --> 00:32:14,040
A resonator within the laser housing channels a direct current

596
00:32:14,140 --> 00:32:19,380
into a glass tube containing gas, like carbon dioxide.

597
00:32:19,480 --> 00:32:23,880
The current excites the gas, which emits photons of light.

598
00:32:23,980 --> 00:32:27,020
It'll actually start off when it comes out of the resonator

599
00:32:27,120 --> 00:32:31,400
at about approximately an inch, inch and a half.

600
00:32:31,500 --> 00:32:34,000
And as it comes down through the laser head,

601
00:32:34,100 --> 00:32:38,540
it hits a focusing lens, and it brings it down into space

602
00:32:38,541 --> 00:32:42,780
point that you can almost not see.

603
00:32:42,880 --> 00:32:44,780
The naked eye sees only the warm glow

604
00:32:44,880 --> 00:32:47,580
of the laser impacting and melting through the steel.

605
00:32:50,080 --> 00:32:52,280
The laser light itself is nearly invisible

606
00:32:52,380 --> 00:32:56,700
because it differs greatly from visible light.

607
00:32:56,800 --> 00:32:59,800
Visible light contains a myriad of wavelengths

608
00:32:59,900 --> 00:33:02,700
and is ultimately scattered and weak.

609
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:05,700
Laser light consists of just a single wavelength.

610
00:33:05,800 --> 00:33:08,540
For this reason, it remains concentrated in the laser.

611
00:33:08,541 --> 00:33:11,280
and powerful.

612
00:33:11,380 --> 00:33:13,780
Passing the light from a 100-watt bulb

613
00:33:13,880 --> 00:33:16,020
through the same laser cutting mechanism

614
00:33:16,120 --> 00:33:19,480
would only focus the beam to a minimum area of 4 tenths of an

615
00:33:19,580 --> 00:33:23,720
inch and an energy level over 4,000 times weaker than that

616
00:33:23,820 --> 00:33:26,660
of the laser.

617
00:33:26,760 --> 00:33:29,460
This one right here is a 1,700-watt laser.

618
00:33:29,560 --> 00:33:33,260
It's approximately 20 million watts per square centimeter

619
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:35,700
is what it's measured as, whereas if you were to measure

620
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:38,300
like a soldering iron, it would be about maybe 100 watts

621
00:33:38,301 --> 00:33:41,040
per square centimeter.

622
00:33:41,140 --> 00:33:43,400
The most powerful lasers can slice through steel

623
00:33:43,500 --> 00:33:46,680
up to an inch and a quarter thick at nearly 60 inches

624
00:33:46,780 --> 00:33:49,420
per minute.

625
00:33:49,520 --> 00:33:51,540
All this is really a sharp cut.

626
00:33:51,640 --> 00:33:53,780
What happens is that the edges are so straight

627
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:54,920
within the laser beam.

628
00:33:55,020 --> 00:33:57,080
On the bottom side, you can see if you feel the bottom,

629
00:33:57,180 --> 00:33:57,980
you have no burr.

630
00:33:58,080 --> 00:33:58,860
There's no dross.

631
00:33:58,960 --> 00:33:59,960
It's real smooth.

632
00:34:00,060 --> 00:34:02,360
It's the same as basically the top side of the cut.

633
00:34:02,460 --> 00:34:04,660
Basically, if you were to take and stand this part straight up

634
00:34:04,661 --> 00:34:09,660
