651
00:35:13,820 --> 00:35:16,300
To create this intensely sharp beam,

652
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:21,140
pressurized gas, like oxygen, is forced through a narrow cavity.

653
00:35:21,240 --> 00:35:24,800
A negatively charged electrode positioned in the cavity center

654
00:35:24,900 --> 00:35:27,740
creates a spark when the plasma cutter nozzle touches the

655
00:35:27,741 --> 00:35:31,040
The plasma cutter nozzle touches the surface of the positively

656
00:35:31,140 --> 00:35:33,740
charged steel plate.

657
00:35:33,840 --> 00:35:37,420
At the atomic level, the extreme heat strips free the gas's

658
00:35:37,520 --> 00:35:39,660
electrons.

659
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:43,180
This ionizes the gas molecules, creating electrically

660
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:47,300
conductive plasma.

661
00:35:47,400 --> 00:35:49,000
As it comes out of the nozzle, it

662
00:35:49,100 --> 00:35:54,000
cuts at about 25,000 to 30,000 degrees.

663
00:35:54,100 --> 00:35:56,940
The plasma is also flowing at up to 22,000 feet

664
00:35:56,941 --> 00:36:01,240
That's fast enough to zip from New York to Los Angeles

665
00:36:01,340 --> 00:36:02,680
in a little over 10 minutes.

666
00:36:05,940 --> 00:36:09,180
So what you're seeing there with the sparks that come out

